WEBVTT

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.350
The next stop is Tokyo. Tokyo.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.770
You are currently on the
Keihin-Tohoku Line, bound for Ofuna.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:09.530
The next stop after Tokyo will be Yurakucho.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.950
JNR is the largest railroad
company in all of Japan.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:26.880
Its railways stretch from Wakkanai, Hokkaido in
the north to Nishioyama, Kagoshima in the south.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.170
All in all, about 25,000 km of steel track.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:35.510
Such a company is made possible by the fact that it is a government-insured,

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.260
virtually untouchable state-owned enterprise.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:47.150
As such, many of those who dream of job stability seek employment there.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.030
This is doubly true of those
who also love the rails.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.440
I would be one such person.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:56.860
My balloon.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.490
Man, that's pretty stuck.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:00.620
Gimme a boost!

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.960
Wow, lady!

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.810
Molester.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.310
Why?!

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:29.690
Hey, are you a JNR OJT applicant too?

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.320
Yes, I am.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.860
Same here!

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:33.860
What a relief.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.990
I don't really know my way around here.
No way...

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.310
I saw you this morning, didn't I?

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:30.390
My name is Haruka Koumi.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:31.890
It's nice to meet you.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:34.770
I'm Naoto Takayama.

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:36.320
Nice to meet you, too.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:38.900
Stand.

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:41.490
Bow!

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.660
Good. You may sit.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:53.960
There is a system of work training in place
at JNR for students, called JNR Student OJT.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:59.210
This year, for some reason all applicants were assigned to the
Railway Public Security Force, regardless of preference.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:03.590
Members of the PSF are required to undergo the Special Public Security Department program

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:06.510
here at JNR Central Academy.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.680
Today is the first day of said program.

00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:14.190
I'm Tokyo Public Security
Riot Police Captain Gonou.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:17.860
I am charged with guiding you
for the next month.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:21.030
You may be trainees,
but don't expect to be babied.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.780
Starting tomorrow, the class
arbiter will be Iwaizumi.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.620
Each subsequent day we will
move down the trainee list in order.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.080
Shou Iwaizumi, are you here?

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.580
That's you, right?

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:37.710
Oh, sorry. Was focusing on my food.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.670
Are you deaf?

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:40.420
Sir!

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.720
Before we start,
allow me to say something.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:47.300
At a railroad company, you are responsible for our customers.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.140
In other words, their lives.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:52.730
On the rails, one wrong decision can lead to tragic accidents.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:56.480
At work you must be
professionals at all times.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.440
Make this your creed.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.900
Furthermore, this is the last time
you will ever make a lazy greeting.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.860
You salute your superior officers!

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.620
Am I speaking French here?

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.620
Sir!

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:09.370
Good.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.790
Now for your training.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.160
Takayama.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:12.790
Yes?

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:19.040
Tell me, if a molester attempts to escape instead of submitting to officers, how should he be dealt with?

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.170
Huh?

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:24.920
Shoot the bastard.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:25.840
What?

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.890
What's the matter, Takayama?

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:30.010
Uh, right!

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.680
Well, um...

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.480
Instructor Gonou!

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:37.650
Yes, Sakurai?

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:40.150
I believe he should be shot and killed!

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.320
What?

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:42.190
Shot?

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.150
Maybe one day that will be legal.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:47.360
I hope that day comes, too.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.070
However, Sakurai, today it isn't.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:51.830
Yes.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.660
I understand, Instructor.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:55.200
It is most unfortunate.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:02.170
And so began my days of chaos, all so I could have my dream job at JNR.

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:08.930
Koumi!

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:13.680
You're always the top scorer on our daily tests. That's amazing.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.680
Oh, it's not really.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.020
You trying to sink your
fangs into Haruka <i>again</i>?

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.850
O-Of course not!

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:21.230
Really?

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.900
'Cuz I could swear your eyes
were glued to her breasts.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:24.860
WhaвЂ”

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:30.740
That's not true! It's not, Koumi!

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:34.240
Haruka, you're just going to lose brain cells talking to this thing.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:35.540
Why?!

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:36.250
Hey.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:41.500
How do you tell that the EF66 is classified as an electric train?

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:46.800
Well, the E in EF stands for Electric.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:52.890
Also, the F is the sixth letter in the alphabet,
so that tells you it has six driving wheels.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.140
I get it!

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:57.600
If you need help studying, I can help a bit.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:01.440
Really?

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:02.440
Yes.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.480
Can you help me, too?

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:05.020
Yeah.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.360
Okay! Let's blow this month of training out of the water!

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:08.820
Yeah!

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:27.130
Takayama!

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:32.390
The Railway Public Security Force is allowed to carry handguns in emergencies.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:36.510
You are all required to fire 50 rounds in target practice a year.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:40.850
In essence, if you can't use
a gun, we cannot accept you.

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:43.440
Now, each of you, begin firing.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:53.280
Keep calm! Steel yourselves!

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.950
Iwaizumi, lower your arms!

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.410
You've got good form,
but you missed every shot.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.000
Koumi!

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.590
Owwie.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:09.090
Are you okay, Koumi?

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.880
You hurt?

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.220
No, it just scared me a bit.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.340
Thank goodness.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:25.860
Sakurai.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.860
Not a single miss.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:28.900
Well done.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.820
But remember to hold the gun
with <i>both</i> hands.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:35.610
So?

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.030
Wanna see who's a better shot?

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:38.530
Why?!

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:45.290
My days of training at JNR Central Academy passed in much this fashion.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:53.590
Soon there were only two days left of getting off at Nishi-Kokubunji Station for our training.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:58.140
Those would be the hardest days
we'd ever experienced.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:04.940
Every single one of our modern railway standards comes from the days of steam-powered locomotives.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:09.480
If you don't understand this, you will never be able to work on a train, be it an electric one

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:11.320
or even the bullet train.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:15.820
As such, you will now be
training in shoveling coal.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.700
You will all be situated in tandem C62's.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.750
You will not pass until you achieve a speed of over 100 km/h.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.380
We can do this, guys.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:33.300
Yeah! I'm gonna pay you all back in full for helping me study!

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.590
Takayama.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.840
Your group's first.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.350
Right!

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.560
So we push on this pedal, andвЂ”

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.440
Whoa, hot!

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.060
I'm getting pumped already!

00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:56.150
And...

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:56.990
Start!

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:59.370
Signal to depart received!

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:00.950
Off we go!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:21.390
Normally, the C62 requires about 100 liters of water and 40 kg of coal to go one kilometer.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:26.930
In order to reach 100 km/h, a sizable amount of coal must be burned.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.960
What's the matter, trainees?

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:56.210
We're not getting nearly enough steam!

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:57.210
R-Right!

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:58.920
No way!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:01.300
What're we at, 500 km/h?

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.760
What do you think this is,
a magnetic rail?

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:03.720
Oh, forget it.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.390
Look, we're peaking at 80 km/h!

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:13.190
Wait...

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:15.690
Iwaizumi, we need fuel efficiency!

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:16.690
Huh?

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:19.950
Fuel efficiency, guys!

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:26.080
Right! We can't just heap in the coal.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:27.410
What're you talking about?

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:29.790
Just shovel where I tell you to.

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:32.000
Now that I understand!

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.380
First, deep to the right.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.290
On it!

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:40.590
See, you can't simply throw coal at a steam locomotive's boiler.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:45.640
You have to increase fuel efficiency by having less coal in the center and more on the edges.

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:48.890
Thus the weapon of choice
is not a great big shovel

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:52.560
but a scoop that can throw coal at precise locations inside the boiler.

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.060
Up close on the left.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.310
Now inner left.

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:56.020
Righto!

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.440
Inner left.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:58.980
Now up close on the right.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:00.860
Now up close on the left.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.660
Now inner right.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:04.030
Now inner left.

00:12:20.210 --> 00:12:21.590
Well done.

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.090
You pass.

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:25.760
Hey, trainees!

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:27.260
You've hit your goal.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.230
We did it!

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:44.490
The most surprising thing was that us four
ended up being the only ones to reach 100 km/h.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:48.080
Stand!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.450
Once your last training session ends tomorrow,

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:56.630
you will all be granted permission to participate in the JNR Student OJT program.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:13:01.340
While you will still be in-training, this does not change the fact that you are out in the field as a PSF officer.

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:05.880
The Public Security Force keeps
JNR's customers safe.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:11.680
Make sure that no matter the reason,
nothing threatens to keep you from doing this.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:12.430
Understood?

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:14.230
Yes, sir!

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:21.440
Our last training with JNR Central Academy was to be an evaluation of our skills in the field.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:25.740
Thus I was stationed in Tokyo.

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:29.950
But somehow the four of us
wound up together again.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:31.450
Pay attention!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:37.500
Let me remind you, you are only amateurs
who have come here for their last day of training.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.790
Don't do anything unnecessary.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:41.340
Just listen to what I tell you!

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:42.420
You, there!

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.880
Why are you dressed like you're
going into a war zone?

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:48.390
This uses ultra-high-density
reinforced FRP fiberвЂ”

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.470
That's not what I was asking!

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:51.970
I'll repeat myself.

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.180
Do not do <i>anything</i> unnecessary.

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:59.860
If any problems spring up, there goes my chance at transferring to the main office.

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:04.360
Yes, hello?

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:07.240
Huh?

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.360
Oh, okay.

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:11.410
I'll send someone.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:13.160
Has there been an incident?

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:15.500
What're you talking about?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:18.370
Someone heard a dog barking in a train.

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:20.080
One of you go deal with it.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:21.340
A dog?

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.800
I'll go.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:25.130
Me too, then.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:30.430
Isn't the Express Hayabusa
with sleeper car awesome?

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:33.310
It's a new model of electric
locomotive, the EF68.

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:37.270
All double-deckers in the
28 series's style of sleeper car.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:39.850
You really like trains, huh?

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:40.900
I do.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:42.860
They're man's best friend!

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:48.780
So, Koumi, why are you
aspiring to work at JNR?

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:49.570
Huh?

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:53.950
Well, I've known you a month, but I just realized we never talked about your reason for being here.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:56.290
Well...

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:01.580
I still think I should be up there.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.000
No, it's okay.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.420
Careful, nowвЂ”

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:05.920
Whoa!

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:06.510
Huh?

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:10.130
Uh, nothing.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:15.510
To answer your question,
there's someone I admire.

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:18.020
And if I join JNR, I'll be able to...

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:20.980
Is that wrong of me?

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:24.270
Not at all. I'm pretty much the same, really.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.480
It's not wrong of you in the least!

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:25.770
Huh?

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:33.740
Watch out!

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:54.550
S-Sorry!

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.180
M-Me too!

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:01.310
You saved me again.

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:02.520
Huh?

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.230
Oh, nothing.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:12.360
Wow, my arms are killing me.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:14.990
But it's so small and cute.

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.240
Weird, huh?

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:18.620
Now we have to fill out this form.

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:23.170
How're we supposed to know the value?

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:27.250
Together it's about 400,000 yen, I'd guess.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:30.590
The pet carrier is from a French brand.

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:33.380
Wow. You sure know a lot.

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:35.590
I thought you seemed like a high-class lady.

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:37.510
This fits you to a tee.

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:39.560
Really?

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:41.140
Don't you go trusting him.

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:43.020
Sakurai!

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:43.890
Iwaizumi!

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:47.520
Men never turn their silver tongues off.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:50.150
Why do you always have to treat guys like they're your sworn enemy?

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:51.650
Because of their egos!

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:54.320
Oh, the chief was pretty pissed.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.320
You guys are taking too long, apparently.

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:56.910
What?

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.120
We have to hurry!

00:16:58.990 --> 00:16:59.740
Huh?

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:03.620
Purse snatchers!

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:04.460
After 'em!

00:17:04.460 --> 00:17:05.000
Right!

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:06.330
Thank you!

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:07.000
No problem!

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:10.670
Get back here!

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:20.100
Iwaizumi, take the next turn!

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.430
We'll cut through the turnstiles
and head them off!

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:23.640
All right!

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.060
This is Takayama!

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:31.110
Get back here, already.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:33.400
We're in pursuit of some purse snatchers at the moment!

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:33.690
What?!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:34.360
Huh?
What?!

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:34.400
Huh?

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:36.280
I told you not to do anything unвЂ”

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:40.370
This is an emergency.
The situation at hand takes priority.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:41.410
Right?

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:49.420
Outta the way!

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:04.930
The historic high-speed Bullet Train Relay bound for Omiya will depart soon.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.270
Please do not try to force
your way onto the train.

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:10.440
Get off, damn you!

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:11.650
Sakurai!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.830
Touchy-feely much?

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:27.910
Ow, ow, ow.

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:31.000
The announcer said that train is headed for Omiya, right?

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:33.130
It'll get there at 1:50 p.m.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:35.670
Huh? You remember the schedule?

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:36.670
All of it?

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:37.840
Yes.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:44.850
To catch it, we'd need to take the
599 bullet train headed for Tohoku.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:48.020
The problem is it left at 1:20 p.m.

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:51.230
And there aren't any more, huh?

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:53.320
But that means they'll just get away!

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:54.730
What can we do?

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:57.940
It's not on the timetable,

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:02.870
but I think there was something on the
special schedule at this morning's meeting.

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.540
Morning meeting? Special schedule?

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.410
I've got it!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:09.290
There's a way to catch them!

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:11.960
What is it? Tell us already!

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:14.710
The Doctor Yellow!

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:20.130
The Bullet Train Electric Rail Test Train,
or Doctor Yellow for short.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:24.550
It runs at 200 km/h, checking the
overhead wiring and rails for problems.

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:32.150
The schedule for this one's not made public, so I've never seen one before.

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.400
Iwaizumi!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:35.070
Heya!

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:36.860
What were you doing?

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:39.530
They got away because
you weren't there toвЂ”

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:41.280
Yeah, I got lost.

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:43.030
No internal compass?

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.990
Just forget it. Let's move!

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:54.330
Thank you again for riding the historic high-speed Bullet Train Relay.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:57.090
We will be arriving at our
last stop, Omiya, shortly.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:20:01.010
The exit for Omiya Station,
track 11 is on the left.

00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:03.260
We've arrived in Omiya.

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:08.100
Uh, hi.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:09.560
Whadda you want?

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:14.770
We're here about a purse snatching that
occurred in Tokyo Station. Would you mind?

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:16.310
What'd you just say?

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:17.610
The hell?

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:21.240
Is JNR treating its customers
like criminals now?

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:23.280
Of course not, sir.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:27.120
We'd just like to ask you
some questions, to be certain.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:31.040
And we're from the Public Security Force.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:34.210
If we catch you red-handed,

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:36.330
we have the authority to arrest you.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:39.920
Under JNR regulations article 9, section 2.

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:41.670
You see?

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.430
So if you wouldn't mind...

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:45.340
Oh?

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.760
That all you wanted to say?

00:21:11.870 --> 00:21:13.370
And that's that!

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:15.120
Damn you!

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.000
No!
Damn you!

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:16.460
Damn you!

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.460
You fools!

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:21.460
How dare you act on your own?

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.380
This is a major problem!

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:27.140
I'll be reporting this to
the higher-ups in full!

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.730
Time to start thinking
about a new job, huh?

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:38.100
We did nothing wrong!

00:21:39.020 --> 00:21:41.110
Um, Takayama...

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.650
Well, bye.

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:45.950
And so, I...

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:50.910
joined the OJT program!

00:21:56.370 --> 00:21:57.460
Okay!

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:00.670
Heya!

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:01.920
Took you long enough.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:02.920
Huh?

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.260
Good to see you again.

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:06.420
I had a feeling this would happen.

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:09.930
Welcome to K4!

00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:43.100
The JNR EF82 electric locomotive is

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:48.490
the successor to EF81, which served for many years as an AC/DC dual-use electric locomotive,

00:23:48.490 --> 00:23:52.610
and is equipped with six RW1
three-phase squirrel-cage induction motors

00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:56.330
that provide enough power
to haul the 1350-ton train!

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:58.620
Enough with the lecture!

00:23:58.620 --> 00:24:01.830
The next episode will feature an NRSAT-exclusive train!

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:05.840
Rail Wars, Episode Two: Just Let Me for a Little.

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:08.800
This jet black body chases down evil!
